---
import WorkingGraph from '../../components/WorkingGraph.jsx';
import published from '../../../public/legacy/0.20260206e/tensor.core.graph.json';
import graph from '../../../public/graphs/working/tensor.core.graph.json';
import criteria from '../../../public/graphs/working/entry-evidence-criteria.json';
import source from '../../../public/core/0.1.0-draft.1/provenance.json';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, seo } from '../../data/seo';

const meta = seo.graphs;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString() || 'https://tensor-standards.pages.dev/';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'TechArticle',
  headline: meta.title,
  description: meta.description,
  url: absoluteUrl(siteUrl, meta.canonicalPath),
};
---

<BaseLayout title={meta.title} description={meta.description} canonicalPath={meta.canonicalPath} ogType={meta.ogType} jsonLd={jsonLd} hidePageTitle>
  <section class="atlas-page" aria-label="Investigation graph workspace">
    <WorkingGraph published={published} graph={graph} criteria={criteria} source={source} client:load />
    <div class="atlas-coverage" id="coverage">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">COVERAGE / AN OPEN MIGRATION</p><h2>Preserved does not mean<br />brought forward.</h2><p>The working draft contains <strong>82 rewritten original IDs and 21 new questions</strong>. <strong>506 original questions are absent</strong> from the active draft. Equivalent investigative coverage has not yet been demonstrated.</p></div>
      <div><div class="atlas-lineage"><div>588<small>Published</small></div><span>→</span><div>219<small>Reduced draft</small></div><span>→</span><div>184<small>Entry repair</small></div><span>→</span><div>103<small>Positive repair</small></div></div><p>Every original question is accounted for in a source-pinned ledger. The next stage reviews each capability, its evidence criteria, routes, and scenarios before restoring or consolidating it.</p><div class="cta-group"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/graphs/coverage/">Coverage ledger &amp; roadmap →</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/questions/">Published catalog</a></div></div>
    </div>
    <noscript><p>The question list and evidence criteria below work without JavaScript. Enable JavaScript for the node canvas and focused inspector.</p></noscript>
    <details class="tensor-panel graph-static-outline"><summary>Complete working graph and criteria · text view</summary><ol>{graph.nodes.map((node) => <li id={`working-${node.id}`}><h3>{node.id} · {node.label}</h3><p>{node.text}</p><dl>{Object.entries(criteria.rules[criteria.nodes[node.id].rule]).map(([answer, text]) => <div><dt>{answer}</dt><dd>{text}</dd></div>)}</dl><ul>{graph.edges.filter((edge) => edge.source === node.id).map((edge) => <li>{edge.decision} → <a href={`#working-${edge.target}`}>{edge.target}</a></li>)}</ul></li>)}</ol></details>
    <details class="tensor-panel graph-static-outline"><summary>Complete published graph · 588 questions · text view</summary><ol>{published.nodes.map((node) => <li id={`published-${node.id}`}><h3>{node.id} · {node.label}</h3><p>{node.text}</p><ul>{published.edges.filter((edge) => edge.source === node.id).map((edge) => <li>{edge.decision} → <a href={`#published-${edge.target}`}>{edge.target}</a></li>)}</ul></li>)}</ol></details>
    <details class="tensor-panel graph-static-outline"><summary>Reference tools &amp; preserved releases</summary><p>Published releases remain unchanged. The atlas replaces the old graph as the main exploration view; historical import and overlay tools remain available.</p><ul><li><a href="/studio/">Archived Graph Studio · import &amp; overlays</a></li><li><a href="/assets/releases/manifest.json">Historical release manifest</a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/tensor-standards-consortium/TENSOR-Framework/tree/main/releases/core/graphs">Published graph archive</a></li><li><a href="/schemas/">Schemas</a> · <a href="/metrics/">Historical structural metrics</a></li></ul><p>Graph structure does not establish evidence truth or investigation effectiveness. Bringing a published question forward requires review of its meaning, bounds, evidence and assessment criteria.</p></details>
    <p class="graph-downloads"><a href="/graphs/working/tensor.core.graph.json" download>Working graph JSON</a> · <a href="/graphs/working/entry-evidence-criteria.json" download>Evidence criteria JSON</a> · <a href="/investigation-lab/">Follow a recorded investigation path</a></p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
.graph-static-outline { padding: 1rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
.graph-static-outline summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent-primary); }
.graph-static-outline ol { padding: 1rem 0 0 1.5rem; }
.graph-static-outline ol > li { padding: 1rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft); scroll-margin-top: 7rem; }
.graph-static-outline dl { margin: .7rem 0; font-size: .85rem; }
.graph-static-outline dt { font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent-primary); }
.graph-static-outline ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
.graph-downloads { margin: 1.2rem 0 2rem; font-size: .9rem; }
</style>
